Maximilian Wu Liang wrote:
> i have a list containing 10000 objects, but a vast majority of them are
> NULL. I need to generate
> a shorter list containing only non-NULL entries, and retain
> corresponding names. is there a loop-less method to quickly accomplish
> this task?
>
> thank you
> max wu

Loopless? No. Vectorized? Yes.

# create a dummy list with NULL elements
x <- vector("list", 10000)
# make the first 20 not NULL
x[1:20] <- 1
length(x) # [1] 10000
# remove NULL elements
y <- x[!sapply(x, is.null)]
length(y) # [1] 20

sapply is still a loop, but perhaps more efficient than for.

--sundar

