From rmh at temple.edu  Wed Jul  6 13:51:36 2005
From: rmh at temple.edu (Richard M. Heiberger)
Date: Wed, 06 Jul 2005 09:51:36 -0400
Subject: Re: Unexpected Memory Problems with samll
Message-ID: <7924f339.17a412f7.81b2800@po-d.temple.edu>

"internal engine connection failure"  means a bug in the S-Plus interpreter.

6.1 is two major releases out of date.  One of the things that gets fixed
between releases is internal bugs.  I would start by suggesting an update
to 7.0.

Additionally, in your applications, 7.0 has a "bigdata" library.
>From the file nsightful/splus70/library/bigdata/readme.txt:

S-PLUS Big Data Library

The S-PLUS Big Data library is a data analysis toolkit designed
specifically for exploring data sets that are too big to fit into
memory. The Big Data library in the S-PLUS Enterprise Developer
edition provides the following features:

* S-PLUS operates on the data binary cache file directly, using
"streaming" techniques, where data flows through the application
rather than being processed all at once in memory. The cache file is
processed on a row-by-row basis, meaning that only a small part of the
data is stored in RAM at any one time. It is this out-of-memory data
processing technique that enables S-PLUS to process data sets hundreds
of megabytes, or even gigabytes, in size without requiring large
quantities of RAM.

