>Dear 
s-list 

>I want to find the 
first consecutive pair with the first value >0 and the second value > 200 
in the following vector: 
>X 
<- c( 204,   -24,   -33,   433, 
-1123,   565,   366,  -494,   
261,   205,  270,   201) 
>So in this case 
index 6 and 7 will be the first event and 9,10; 10,11 and 11,12 the others. I 
want only to select the first time this condition occurs in the 
vector

>Any ideas in how to do it the easy way? 

>Thanks 

>Andries 

Dear Andries,
A function that does that is:

find1<-
function(X, b1 = 0, b2 = 200)
{
        s1 
<- 1:(length(X) - 1)
        s2 
<- s1 + 1
        res1 
<- s1[X[s1] > b1 & X[s2] > b2][1]
        c(res1, 
res1 + 1)
}

Best wishes, 
Mario

